5.Imagine you executed your test cases and found 2 bugs. Write defect reports for both, including steps to reproduce, expected vs actual results, and severity. Then, prepare a brief final test report summarizing your testing process and results.
Answer :

Defect Report 1 – Payment Failure

Defect ID: BUG-01
Title: Payment fails even with valid payment details
Severity: High

Steps to Reproduce:
1>Login to the Zomato app.
2>Select a restaurant and add food to the cart.
3>Proceed to checkout.
4>Select UPI payment.
5>Enter valid payment details and confirm payment.

Expected Result:
Payment should be completed successfully and the order should be confirmed.

Actual Result:
Payment fails and the order is not confirmed even though valid payment details are used.

Defect Report 2 – Incorrect Cart Total

Defect ID: BUG-02
Title: Cart total is incorrect after removing an item
Severity: Medium

Steps to Reproduce:
1>Select a restaurant.
2>Add Pizza (₹250) and Burger (₹150).
3>Open the cart.
4>Remove the Burger.

Expected Result:
The cart total should update to ₹250.

Actual Result:
The cart continues to display ₹400 after removing the Burger.

>>Final Test Report

Application: Zomato-like Food Delivery App
Features Tested: Food ordering, cart, coupon, and payment.

Manual testing was performed using positive and negative test cases. 8 test cases were executed and 2 defects were identified. One high-severity defect was found in payment and one medium-severity defect was found in cart calculation.

Test Result: Testing is not fully passed because the payment defect should be fixed and retested before release.
